Hard-won Figma Plugin-API traps. **Read this BEFORE writing any `use_figma` code** — async/font rules,
binding completeness, swap/clone detachment, variant-picker failures, the `VariableID:` prefix trap.
The full set (Gotchas #1–#29) lives in the DS source; the studio context relies most on these:

| Gotcha | Why the studio context cares |
|---|---|
| #1 | load all fonts before ANY text op |
| #16 | screen scroll: chrome at END, `numberOfFixedChildren` counts from the end |
| #20 | consumer instances cache old layout until swapped — the heart of `rebind` |
| #21 | `swapComponent` resets vector fills → re-bind colored glyphs after every swap |
| #27 | binding completeness must be AUDITED, not assumed (zero unbound color is the gate) |
| #28 | clone/swap detach property refs; property defaults are SHARED across variants |
| #29 | `getVariableByIdAsync` needs the `VariableID:` prefix; a bare id silently no-ops |

These are referenced by name throughout `skills/screens.md` and the `rebind` skill — keep this mirror
fresh so those references resolve to the current canon.

